# XSH asctime()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# asctime_r() and ctime_r() were removed in Issue 8 (the page, shared with
# them, no longer describes them), so only asctime() is tested. Members
# outside their normal ranges and years outside 1000 to 9999 are undefined
# and not used. The shared static buffer is read before the next call.

assertion  XSH.asctime.001
anchor     functions/asctime.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/asctime.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       asctime() returns a pointer to the 26-byte string of the form
           weekday, month, day, hours:minutes:seconds, year and a newline:
           for second 52, minute 3, hour 1, day 16, month September, year
           1973, Sunday, it is "Sun Sep 16 01:03:52 1973" plus a newline.
test       t/001-example.c

assertion  XSH.asctime.002
anchor     functions/asctime.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       The day of the month is printed in a field of width two, padded on
           the left with a space for 1 to 9 and not padded for 10 to 31.
test       t/002-day-padding.c

assertion  XSH.asctime.003
anchor     functions/asctime.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       The weekday abbreviation is chosen by tm_wday (Sun to Sat) and the
           month abbreviation by tm_mon (Jan to Dec), independently of each
           other and of the day.
test       t/003-names.c

assertion  XSH.asctime.004
anchor     functions/asctime.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       Hour, minute and second are each printed as two digits with a
           leading zero.
test       t/004-time-digits.c

assertion  XSH.asctime.005
anchor     functions/asctime.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       The year printed is 1900 plus tm_year, as four decimal digits, for
           years 1000 to 9999.
test       t/005-year.c
